      "text": "string of his tongue was loosed, Mark 7:35. they shall speak with new tongues, Mark 16:17. all … began to speak with other tongues, Acts 2:4. they spake with tongues, Acts 19:6. to another divers kinds of tongues, 1 Cor. 12:10. Though I speak with the tongues of men and of angels, 1 Cor. 13:1 (2 Ne. 31:13). whether there be tongues, they shall cease, 1 Cor. 13:8. he that speaketh in an unknown tongue speaketh … unto God, 1 Cor. 14:2. tongues are for a sign … to them that believe not, 1 Cor. 14:22. bridleth not his tongue … this man’s religion is vain, James 1:26. tongue is a little member, and boasteth great things, James 3:5. tongue is a fire, a world of iniquity, James 3:6. tongue can no man tame, James 3:8. Thou must prophesy again before … nations, and tongues, Rev. 10:11 (11:9; 13:7).",
